WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.665 --> 00:00:02.999
- Like my grandfather
Jacques Cousteau used to say

00:00:02.999 --> 00:00:06.587
the impossible missions are
the only ones that succeed.

00:00:06.587 --> 00:00:09.734
And before humankind
had explored the moon

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:12.841
my family set out to explore the sea.

00:00:12.841 --> 00:00:15.939
That's why they launched the
Continental Shelf Initiative,

00:00:15.939 --> 00:00:18.521
a series of underwater
research laboratories,

00:00:18.521 --> 00:00:22.188
the likes of which the
world had never seen.

00:00:33.696 --> 00:00:38.336
In 1960, my grandfather joined
by my father Philippe Sr.

00:00:38.336 --> 00:00:41.344
set out to build an underwater
research station for

00:00:41.344 --> 00:00:43.921
their growing team of oceanauts.

00:00:43.921 --> 00:00:46.019
They were kind of like you guys.

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:48.994
Two years later Conshelf
was dropped at a depth

00:00:48.994 --> 00:00:52.420
of about 30 feet off
the coast of Marseille.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:56.587
A yellow steel cylinder, 16
feet long and 8 feet in diameter

00:00:57.669 --> 00:01:01.756
it served as a home and
lab for its two inhabitants

00:01:01.756 --> 00:01:02.589
for a week.

00:01:02.589 --> 00:01:05.535
A short time later
Conshelf II was dropped onto

00:01:05.535 --> 00:01:09.702
a reef in the Red Sea, where
we find ourselves today.

00:01:13.065 --> 00:01:15.969
Not only was Conshelf
a research platform for

00:01:15.969 --> 00:01:17.646
marine scientists.

00:01:17.646 --> 00:01:20.492
- It was also a human
experiment to test the effects

00:01:20.492 --> 00:01:23.718
of isolation and sun deprivation.

00:01:23.718 --> 00:01:26.358
- [Blond Man] Six oceanauts
spent a month living at

00:01:26.358 --> 00:01:28.358
depths of up to 82 feet.

00:01:29.725 --> 00:01:34.144
Nowadays, Conshelf II,
covered in coral and algae

00:01:34.144 --> 00:01:37.247
is teeming with lionfish, clownfish,

00:01:37.247 --> 00:01:39.164
and beautiful anemones.

00:01:40.622 --> 00:01:44.262
The experiment proved that
explorers can live underwater

00:01:44.262 --> 00:01:47.060
for protracted periods of time.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:51.227
But that the lack of sunlight
made them a little bit loopy.

00:01:54.789 --> 00:01:58.804
- [Male Voice] How long
have we been down here?

00:01:58.804 --> 00:02:00.304
- I've lost track.

00:02:02.972 --> 00:02:04.500
I guess you could say these submarines

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.000
are better suited for animals than people.

00:02:08.944 --> 00:02:10.861
- We are people, right?

